### Goal Model Design Based on Mission Description

The goal model is structured to reflect the mission's requirements, decomposing the mission into hierarchical goals and tasks. The model ensures that each goal and task is clearly defined, with appropriate runtime annotations and relationships.

---

### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                                                                                                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type  | Relation |
|---------|-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|------------|----------|
| G1      | Fulfill Resource Request    | Ensure the requested resources are collected from storage and delivered to the specified location.                                                                                                     | -                 | Perform    | -        |
| G2      | Collect Required Resources  | Gather all required resources from their respective storage locations, considering waiting times and paths.                                                                                       | ;                 | Perform    | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Collected Resources | Transport the collected resources to the specified location, ensuring timely delivery while managing battery levels and potential handover to other robots.                                         | -                 | Perform    | G1       |
| G4      | Recharge Robot Battery      | Return to the recharging station when the battery level drops to 10% during the collection phase.                                                                                                    | -                 | Achieve    | G2       |
| G5      | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Delegate the remaining collection tasks to another robot when the current robot's battery is low.                                                                                                  | -                 | Perform    | G2       |
| G6      | Return Resources to Checkpoint | Transfer resources to a designated checkpoint and assign the remaining delivery task to another robot when the battery level drops to 30% during the delivery phase.                             | -                 | Perform    | G3       |
| G7      | Trigger Resource Alert      | Send an alert and report to the sector manager if a robot fails to return resources to a checkpoint.                                                                                                | -                 | Achieve    | G3       |

---

### Tasks Table

| Task ID | Task Title                       | Text                                                                                                                                                                                                 | Relation | Location                  | Number of Robots |
|---------|----------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|---------------------------|------------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage             | Move to the storage location where the requested resources are stored.                                                                                                                               | AND      | Storage Facility          | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Request Resources               | Communicate with the storage system to retrieve the precise resources needed.                                                                                                                      | AND      | Storage Facility          | 1                |
| AT3     | Deliver to Specified Location   | Transport the collected resources to the specified delivery location.                                                                                                                                | AND      | Delivery Location         | 1                |
| AT4     | Recharge at Station             | Return to the recharging station to replenish the battery.                                                                                                                                          | AND      | Recharging Station        | 1                |
| AT5     | Handover Mission                | Transfer the mission status and resource information to another robot for continuation of the task.                                                                                              | AND      | Current Location          | 1                |
| AT6     | Return to Checkpoint            | Bring the resources back to a designated checkpoint when the battery is low.                                                                                                                        | AND      | Checkpoint                | 1                |
| AT7     | Send Resource Alert             | Trigger an alert and notify the sector manager about the failed resource transfer.                                                                                                                   | AND      | Sector Manager's Office   | 1                |

---

### Logical Relationships

- **G1** -> G2, G3 [AND]: Both collection and delivery are required to fulfill the mission.
- **G2** -> G4, G5 [OR]: Either recharging or assigning to another robot is sufficient to continue the collection phase.
- **G3** -> G6, G7 [OR]: Either returning resources to a checkpoint or triggering an alert is necessary if delivery is interrupted.
- **G4** -> AT1, AT2 [AND]: After recharging, the robot must navigate and request resources again.
- **G5** -> AT3, AT4 [AND]: The assigned robot must deliver and recharge if needed.
- **G6** -> AT5, AT6 [AND]: The robot must handover and return resources to a checkpoint.

---

This goal model effectively captures the mission requirements, ensuring that all tasks are coordinated and executed appropriately, with fallback mechanisms for battery management and resource handling.
